# Keeps `gcloud builds submit` uploads small and, more importantly, keeps
# local-only files out of the image. The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` in the
# builder stage, so anything not listed here ends up in a layer — including
# files that are gitignored and therefore easy to forget about.

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
.next
out
build

# Local credentials and config. NOT secrets today (project ids, a billing
# account id), but they have no business in a container image and this is the
# file that stops them getting there.
#
# `.env*` deliberately, not an enumerated list: the Dockerfile passes every
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* value as a build ARG, so no .env file is ever needed inside the
# image, and a glob cannot be outgrown by a new .env.<something> later.
.env*

# Terraform state, variables, and backend config. terraform.tfvars carries the
# billing account id; backend.hcl names the state bucket.
terraform
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
backend.hcl

# Everything .gitignore keeps out of the repo must stay out of the image too.
# CI builds from a clean checkout where these do not exist, but a local
# `docker build` or `gcloud builds submit` runs in a working tree that has
# them — and `COPY . .` would bake in the shelter's paper register (an
# adopter's name, phone and home coordinates), real animal photos and
# service-account files. Keep this block at least as strict as .gitignore.
_files
_local
_e2e
seed
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
*-service-account*.json
serviceAccountKey.json
.firebaserc.local
ui-debug.log

# VCS and tooling.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Docs and design assets — not needed at runtime or build time.
docs
design
*.md

# Firebase CLI local artefacts.
.firebase
firebase-debug.log
firestore-debug.log

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
